# Fork additions. Everything above is upstream's own ignore list, kept intact
# and unedited, in its original order. No pattern above swallows a Zig path:
# `/build/` is anchored at this root and names a directory that does not exist
# here, so it does not match `build.zig` or `consumer/build.zig`; `/src/tests`
# names the binary upstream's own makefile writes into `src/`, which this build
# never does, because it puts every artifact in the cache tree; and upstream
# lists neither dot-directories nor subdirectories wholesale.
#
# `zig build` creates these directories at the repository root. They are build
# products, so they stay out of commits, and neither appears in the `.paths`
# allowlist in build.zig.zon, so an ordinary user build cannot change the
# package hash.
.zig-cache/
zig-cache/
zig-out/
zig-pkg/

# `consumer/` is a package in its own right: `zig build run` inside it creates
# its own output tree. It is listed here so that a run from the repository root
# cannot be committed by accident. An operator who redirects the cache with
# --cache-dir owns that path instead.
consumer/.zig-cache/
consumer/zig-cache/
consumer/zig-out/
consumer/zig-pkg/
